{
  "about": [
    "Which server URLs a credential of a provider without a fixed host (Ollama, LM Studio, Azure OpenAI) may carry,",
    "and that a request to that server then passes. Plain http only to a loopback host (localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1])",
    "and only for the local servers; never user:password, a query or a fragment.",
    "One list for all wallets: packages/core/tests/proxy-utils.test.ts (resolveProviderBaseUrl, validateProxyUrl),",
    "packages/ios/ByokyTests/ProviderURLTests.swift (Provider.customBaseUrl, validateUrl) and",
    "packages/android/.../proxy/UpstreamPolicyTest.kt (CredentialBaseUrl.normalize, UpstreamPolicy.target),",
    "so a backup opens with the same credentials everywhere. \"request\", when present, must be accepted for that",
    "base URL. Android's network security config allows cleartext to the same three hosts. Add new cases here."
  ],
